[h2]0.8.6[/h2]
[h3]Compatibility fixes[/h3]
[list]
[*]Fixed the new-game crash with Chill Mode and other mod-added game modes. Radioactive tides now follow each mode's weather difficulty; Easy, Normal and Hard keep their existing settings.
[*]Packages now include the macOS asset bundle, fixing missing bundled materials and assets on Mac, including DFArtTimber.
[/list]

[h3]Mining and recovery[/h3]
[list]
[*]The Deep Drill consumes 3 water to extract 1 deep ore from a source in its district. Haulers no longer carry ore directly out of sources or back into them.
[*]Empty Deep Ore Sources recharge 20 ore every 5 days, with a visible cooldown. This is a slow emergency supply; the Deep Mine remains the sustainable industrial source.
[*]Deep Mines use metal block drill bits and brick shaft lining, avoiding a dependency on their own ore output or active quarries.
[*]The Radioactive Water Outfall can dispose of contaminated water. The Reactor Charging Bay now unlocks alongside reactor power cells at 300,000 science.
[/list]

[h3]Buildings and connections[/h3]
[list]
[*]The Hospital no longer requires alloy or machine cores; it uses metal blocks, deep iron and steel instead.
[*]The Technical School's supply panel and stock limits follow the selected profession. Supplies left over after a change are hauled out.
[*]Power shafts and pipe valves can connect to flat walls under shallow roof eaves and to walls with recessed panels.
[*]Connections that intersect moving machinery have been removed. [b]Existing shafts or valves at these spots disconnect; reattach them at a neighbouring connection.[/b]
[*][b]Two Launch Pad roof tiles and two Radioactive Waste Refinery roof tiles no longer support construction[/b] because moving parts cross them. Structures already on these tiles may be removed when the save loads.
[/list]
